WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.910
Gone are the days of endlessly searching video
stores for some undiscovered gem.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.930
Instead, it's all about endlessly scrolling
through Netflix in search of something fresh

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.090
and new to watch.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.099
It's hard to tell what's good or not, so here
are some overlooked comedies from the past

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:20.359
few decades that are just as good as if not
better than all those big, broad blockbusters.

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:22.430
Casa de Mi Padre

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:27.050
Despite being an A-list movie star, Will Ferrell
isn't usually one to rest on his laurels and

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.020
do the same thing over and over again.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.839
He likes to innovate and make good comedy
that interests him, and if other people like

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:34.059
it, great.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:35.829
This is one of those kinds of movies.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:40.969
Casa de Mi Padre is an exercise in both comic
tenacity and silliness, as it's a parody of

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.360
a telenovela and is filmed almost entirely
in Spanish.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:56.629
It should be noted that Ferrell, as a noble
rancher in Mexico, doesn't speak Spanish all

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:00.729
that well as he deals with both an untrustworthy
brother and a fearsome drug lord.

00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:02.160
But that's all part of the comedy.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.560
Goon

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.180
Seann William Scott has been largely relegated
to bully and sidekick roles, such as Stifler

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.299
in the American Pie series and as Chester
in Dude, Where's My Car?.

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:24.469
In Goon, he's front, center, and often bloody
as the star of this charming hockey comedy.

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:28.429
Scott plays Doug, a dumb but good-natured
guy who works as a bouncer but doesn't really

00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:29.820
know what to do with his life.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.680
"Doug did not follow in the family vocation,
he's.."

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.780
"I bounced"

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.020
"Like a basketball?"

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:41.020
Then he discovers he has a knack for being
a hockey enforcer or "goon," the guy who violently

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.899
body-checks opposing players.

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:47.640
Goon was written by Superbad co-writer Evan
Goldberg and Knocked Up star Jay Baruchel,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.080
who co-stars as Scott's best friend.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.080
Little Evil

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.600
Part light-hearted comedy, part horror movie
about the rise of a new antichrist, Little

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.460
Evil mashes up elements of The Omen with domestic
hijinks about a newly married, sensitive modern

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.759
man trying his hardest to bond with his wife's
dark and withdrawn young son.

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:08.920
Gary just can't seem to get five-year-old
Lucas to open up to him.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:15.680
"I'm sure it feels like we've been moving
really fast but I'm your step-father now"

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.200
"Get out."

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.950
As it turns out, Lucas's strange ways are
nature, not nurture his biological dad is

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:27.709
the actual devil but Gary will do whatever
it takes to fend off the forces of evil when

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:30.950
Satan wants Lucas back to trigger the end
of the world.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:36.379
"He's not Satan he's just a portal to Satan
and good parenting it's about keeping that

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:37.379
portal shut."

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:41.530
You know, your typical blended family stuff,
just with a touch of evil incarnate.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:46.760
"I'm sorry I buried you in the backyard … That's
alright.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.760
I get it."

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.280
Masterminds

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.260
Usually, movies that are based on a true story
are dramas.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.239
But sometimes life is a little more absurd,
such as the circumstances that led to the

00:02:56.239 --> 00:03:00.980
1997 robbery of millions from cash handling
company Loomis Fargo.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.360
As demonstrated by the events of Masterminds,
it wasn't exactly the crime of the century.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.220
A petty criminal named Steve convinces his
girlfriend Kelly to plan the heist by romancing

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:15.379
David, a mild-mannered Loomis Fargo driver,
into being their inside man and point man.

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:19.950
David makes a ton of mistakes in the lead-up
to the robbery, the robbery itself, and its

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:20.940
aftermath.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.600
"Gonna put a cap in their ass…

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.700
OH OH DAVID!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.269
Oh that burns"

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:33.890
All in all, it's a goofy crime caper where
absolutely nothing goes right, which means

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.510
it's okay to laugh.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.019
The Trip to Italy

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:42.219
This low-key comedy originated as a BBC series
which was later edited into a feature film,

00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:44.640
just like the two prequels that preceded it.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.110
The Trip documented Steve Coogan and Rob Brydon
taking a restaurant tour of northern England,

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.689
while the plots of The Trip to Spain and The
Trip to Italy are self-explanatory.

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:56.219
The series peaks with the Italian version.

00:03:56.219 --> 00:04:00.159
The British actors and comedians play heightened,
more callous versions of themselves.

00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:04.080
They make fun of each other, each other's
work, and engage in semi-improvised comedy

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.700
bits as they scarf down handmade pasta in
one tiny roadside eatery after another.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:14.310
"Steve's having a little sleep have a drink,
so ah… at his age he needs a nap after lunch

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.150
so ah… he gets confused."

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.570
Adding to the comedy and the lost-in-paradise
vibe is that neither Coogan or Brydon knows

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.260
much of anything about food.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.320
Bachelorette

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.980
This indie ensemble comedy might seem like
a Bridesmaids knock-off, but while it concerns

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.950
a small group of close-knit friends leading
up to a wedding, it actually tells an uncomfortable

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.640
story about people reckoning with the awful
things they did in the past.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:40.420
Three friends reunite to attend the wedding
of their old friend Becky, and they're more

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.810
than a little resentful that the one they
used to make fun of beat them to the altar.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.980
As the wedding draws closer, many embarrassing
secrets are shared, and the main cast also

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.310
manages to get up to some cringe-inducing
slapstick.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.110
But hey, this is a comedy about going to a
wedding, so you can be sure that almost everything

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.250
is patched up by the end.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.250
The Polka King

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:05.200
Finally, a movie about a greedy, street-smart
hustler that also involves polka!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.070
That's The Polka King, a true story that's
so incredibly ridiculous that it could only

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.560
be presented as a comedy.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.660
Jack Black is perfectly cast as Jan Lewan...

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:14.580
"So which one is it, Yan or Jan?"

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.580
"It's whatever you want."

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.460
"Which one is it?"

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.340
"I don't know."

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.720
a polka band leader and entrepreneur who's

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.620
only real crime is a blind adherence to the
American Dream…well, that and fraud.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:31.550
"In Poland everybody do bribes.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:32.550
Do you do bribes?"

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:37.180
In addition to his band, Lewan runs a gift
shop and a record label, only he can't quite

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.400
pay the bills.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.020
After a chance meeting with an elderly couple
who want to invest in his secretly failing

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.840
enterprise, he starts selling securities with
an impossibly good rate of return.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.020
But he doesn't stop there, and his antics
eventually involve millions of ill-gotten

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.020
dollars.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.460
"Ziggy zaggy ziggy zaggy, oy oy oy"

